Phase 2: Core data model + CRUD for campaigns/candidates/sources

Data model (spec §7) — 20 tables, 12 enums, all live in Railway Postgres:

  app/models/base.py        Base + UUIDPrimaryKeyMixin + TimestampMixin
                            + Postgres naming convention
  app/models/enums.py       QualificationType, QualificationStatus, SourceType,
                            AccessMethod, AgentType, PipelineStatus,
                            AgentRunStatus, OutreachChannel, OutreachDirection,
                            OutreachStatus, Language, CampaignStatus
  app/models/auth.py        User, Role  (incl. password_hash on User as the
                            sole sensible deviation from spec — auth needs it)
  app/models/recruiting.py  Campaign, Candidate, CampaignCandidate,
                            CandidateQualification
  app/models/sourcing.py    LeadSource, SourceMention, SchoolProgram,
                            RecruitingEvent
  app/models/operations.py  AgentRun, OutreachEvent, Note
  app/models/knowledge.py   KnowledgeDocument, AssistantQuery
  app/models/settings.py    BrandSettings, LLMSettings, EmailSettings
                            (api keys stored by secret-name reference, never inline)
  app/models/audit.py       AuditLog, RetentionJob
  app/models/__init__.py    full registry exposed for Alembic + app

Migration:
  alembic/versions/a51a71ba6885_initial_schema.py
    - autogenerated from models, both upgrade() and downgrade() populated
    - applied to Railway dev Postgres (acela.proxy.rlwy.net:42839)
    - 21 tables now live (20 app + alembic_version)
  alembic/env.py updated to import app.models so autogenerate sees them

Seed data (spec §14 Phase 2):
  scripts/seed.py — idempotent, safe to re-run
    - 3 RBAC roles: admin, recruiter, viewer
    - 1 brand_settings row with placeholder colors per spec §13

CRUD endpoints (spec §9 — campaigns, candidates, sources):
  app/api/routes/campaigns.py   POST/GET-list/GET-id/PATCH/DELETE
  app/api/routes/candidates.py  + filters: pipeline_status, region
  app/api/routes/sources.py     + filters: source_type, allowed_to_scrape

Pydantic schemas (app/schemas/{campaign,candidate,source}.py):
  - Base/Create/Update/Read pattern per resource
  - EmailStr validation on candidate.contact_email
  - HttpUrl validation on lead_source.url
  - Enums passed through from app.models.enums (single source of truth)

Hard rules honored:
  - LeadSource.allowed_to_scrape defaults to False at the DB level
  - No hardcoded provider names in business logic
  - Foreign-key cascade rules per spec (ON DELETE CASCADE / SET NULL)
  - Audit table is INSERT-only (created_at, no updated_at)

Phase 1 verification still passing — 3 baseline tests preserved.
Phase 2 adds 7 new end-to-end CRUD tests against live Railway:
  - test_campaign_crud_roundtrip
  - test_candidate_requires_identifier
  - test_candidate_crud_roundtrip
  - test_source_crud_roundtrip_and_scrape_flag_defaults_false
  - test_get_unknown_id_returns_404 (parametrized across campaigns/candidates/sources)

Total: 10/10 passing in ~4.4s.

Note: auth gating arrives in Phase 3. Phase 2 endpoints are open by design
so the data path can be verified end-to-end first.

